- **ch22 (first draft heavy — the dairy argument tracked the source's sequence most closely):** Brom's three sentences recast ("Win the sittings. Keep a box."); his box contents and "not much for a box"; Cael's receipts reordered from Denvash forward, Umber named, the "text held / true record on a counter" sentences replaced; Lira's "It's working now?" removed (Cael pre-empts the objection); Brom's "if the code doesn't have one" removed; Karis's induction re-said ("Every rule anybody ever broke looked exactly like this the evening before"); Lira's Fenmark details and "check the ground" → joists and "look underneath"; the tea finding, lamp, and "in four months… the night we decided" → the slow kettle, counting cups, "Memory improves things"; Seln's window posting list, "who decided… since when", the column-of-the-circle list (it mirrored the source's girl/researcher/big one/boy order) → the dairy step and the lamp he held; "arguing with a malfunction" dropped as a sentence. Final 2% / 14% (the 2% is the two packet lines).
